  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44246194",
      "title": "The use() Hook In Action",
      "sourceHash": "51a011006275c6e5499613b68f84fbde304eb0eaf940d45e4eb55b11c9555578",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.248,
          "end": 3.21,
          "en": "[Maximilian Schwarzmüller] So at this point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.21,
          "end": 5.55,
          "en": "we're still not using this use hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.55,
          "end": 8.88,
          "en": "Instead, we have a server component with async await",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.88,
          "end": 11.64,
          "en": "and that works with Suspense, which is great.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.64,
          "end": 12.813,
          "en": "That's good to know.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.92,
          "end": 16.38,
          "en": "But when would we need this use hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.38,
          "end": 17.913,
          "en": "that's built into React?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.75,
          "end": 23.75,
          "en": "Well, let's say UsePromiseDemo for some reason,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.91,
          "end": 26.103,
          "en": "must be a client component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.12,
          "end": 31.65,
          "en": "Because we also want to useState in here, let's say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.65,
          "end": 34.08,
          "en": "Let's say we have a counter here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.08,
          "end": 36.42,
          "en": "Of course, this is kind of a made up example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.42,
          "end": 40.38,
          "en": "but it is just an example to get my point across.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.38,
          "end": 42.45,
          "en": "Let's say we have a counter here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.45,
          "end": 45.303,
          "en": "and we therefore have a button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.32,
          "end": 48.63,
          "en": "which says Increment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.63,
          "end": 50.25,
          "en": "And there upon a click,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.25,
          "end": 52.95,
          "en": "just as we did it earlier in the section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.95,
          "end": 55.29,
          "en": "I want to update my count",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.29,
          "end": 57.57,
          "en": "and I do that by using my previous count",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.57,
          "end": 59.433,
          "en": "and adding one to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.6,
          "end": 65.34,
          "en": "And then I also have a span here where I output that count.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.34,
          "end": 67.56,
          "en": "So we have this code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.56,
          "end": 70.89,
          "en": "And therefore, we need this to be a client component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.89,
          "end": 73.803,
          "en": "And therefore, this won't work anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.85,
          "end": 77.34,
          "en": "Because now we're using server-side code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.34,
          "end": 78.75,
          "en": "in a client component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.75,
          "end": 80.82,
          "en": "And we're trying to use async here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 80.82,
          "end": 83.523,
          "en": "which also doesn't work for client components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 84.57,
          "end": 86.91,
          "en": "So now we actually have to remove async",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 86.91,
          "end": 89.13,
          "en": "and we have to grab that code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.13,
          "end": 92.013,
          "en": "and bring that back into our page.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 92.91,
          "end": 95.913,
          "en": "And also bring back that import here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.52000000000001,
          "end": 99.35300000000001,
          "en": "like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.83,
          "end": 102,
          "en": "Now of course, with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102,
          "end": 104.22,
          "en": "we have the users in the page.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.22,
          "end": 105.93,
          "en": "and we could again pass them down",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 105.93,
          "end": 108.33,
          "en": "to the UsePromiseDemo component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 108.33,
          "end": 110.673,
          "en": "by passing them as props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 111.9,
          "end": 115.743,
          "en": "so that just as before, we accept the users props here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 116.7,
          "end": 120.54,
          "en": "And it looks like I accidentally removed useState here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 120.54,
          "end": 122.73,
          "en": "Of course, we do need that here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 122.73,
          "end": 127.56700000000001,
          "en": "We need count and setCount like this here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 128.67,
          "end": 131.98,
          "en": "in our UsePromisesDemo.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 132.87,
          "end": 135.3,
          "en": "and actually remove that from the homepage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 135.3,
          "end": 137.043,
          "en": "I don't want that there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 137.91,
          "end": 139.35,
          "en": "Here, I just wanna have to code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 139.35,
          "end": 142.77,
          "en": "for having that delay and fetching that data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 142.77,
          "end": 146.463,
          "en": "But with that, if you save that, this works again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 147.78,
          "end": 150.27,
          "en": "But if you copy this and open a new page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 150.27,
          "end": 151.65,
          "en": "we're back to the old state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 151.65,
          "end": 154.023,
          "en": "where the entire page takes two seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 155.01,
          "end": 157.53,
          "en": "Because even though we're using Suspense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 157.53,
          "end": 160.05,
          "en": "the slow part is in this home component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 160.05,
          "end": 163.05,
          "en": "not in the component that's wrapped by Suspense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 163.05,
          "end": 165.873,
          "en": "So Suspense doesn't really help us here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 167.13,
          "end": 171.36,
          "en": "And that's now where the use hook can come in handy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 171.36,
          "end": 176.36,
          "en": "Because what we can do now is create a promise here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 176.4,
          "end": 178.083,
          "en": "in the server component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 179.13,
          "end": 184.02,
          "en": "And pass that promise as a prop to the client component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 184.02,
          "end": 186.12,
          "en": "Yes, this is something you can do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 186.12,
          "end": 188.193,
          "en": "And then use the use hook there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 189.51,
          "end": 190.38,
          "en": "Now for that to work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 190.38,
          "end": 193.38,
          "en": "I'll just need to restructure this a bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 193.38,
          "end": 198.09,
          "en": "and I'll store this promise here in a constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 198.09,
          "end": 200.57999999999998,
          "en": "And when the timeout expires,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 200.57999999999998,
          "end": 203.04,
          "en": "I'll actually set up a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 203.04,
          "end": 207.16,
          "en": "in which I then fetch the data from that file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 208.26,
          "end": 210.567,
          "en": "and where I then call resolve(users),",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 212.737,
          "end": 215.85,
          "en": "so that I have one promise that has a delay,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 215.85,
          "end": 219.06,
          "en": "but that then after that delay expires,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 219.06,
          "end": 220.953,
          "en": "also fetches some data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 222.27,
          "end": 224.59,
          "en": "And now we can pass this fetchUsersPromise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 226.35,
          "end": 227.883,
          "en": "to this users prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 229.5,
          "end": 231.9,
          "en": "And in the UsePromisesDemo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 231.9,
          "end": 234.9,
          "en": "users now gets a promise as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 234.9,
          "end": 238.65,
          "en": "And therefore to get our users that we want an output,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 238.65,
          "end": 241.143,
          "en": "we have to use this use hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 242.52,
          "end": 244.503,
          "en": "which is imported from React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 245.34,
          "end": 248.403,
          "en": "And I'll name my prop here, usersPromise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 250.628,
          "end": 252.75,
          "en": "And therefore, also change that name here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 252.75,
          "end": 255.633,
          "en": "in the page.js file to avoid confusion.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 256.59,
          "end": 260.61,
          "en": "And my users are then the result of calling use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 260.61,
          "end": 262.923,
          "en": "on that usersPromise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 264.63,
          "end": 268.32,
          "en": "And this will then wait for that promise to resolve",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 268.32,
          "end": 269.61,
          "en": "on the client side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 269.61,
          "end": 272.7,
          "en": "And it will integrate with Suspense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 272.7,
          "end": 274.86,
          "en": "so that the fallback is shown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 274.86,
          "end": 278.58299999999997,
          "en": "whilst that data is resolved on the client side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 280.65,
          "end": 282.15,
          "en": "So with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 282.15,
          "end": 284.4,
          "en": "if I copy this and again, open a new page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 284.4,
          "end": 285.57,
          "en": "the page loads instantly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 285.57,
          "end": 289.38,
          "en": "we see the fallback and then this component appears.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 289.38,
          "end": 292.2,
          "en": "But this now is a client component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 292.2,
          "end": 293.7,
          "en": "but a client component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 293.7,
          "end": 296.76,
          "en": "that waits for data with that use hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 296.76,
          "end": 300.693,
          "en": "And that's also something you can do with that use hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 301.8,
          "end": 305.49,
          "en": "It is however a feature that as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 305.49,
          "end": 308.7,
          "en": "does not work in all React projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 308.7,
          "end": 312.99,
          "en": "Instead, this use hook only works when you use promises",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 312.99,
          "end": 315.09,
          "en": "that are created by libraries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 315.09,
          "end": 318.99,
          "en": "that integrate with React's Suspense feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 318.99,
          "end": 321.42,
          "en": "or if you use it on promises",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 321.42,
          "end": 324.15,
          "en": "that are created in a server component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 324.15,
          "end": 328.47,
          "en": "and that are then passed to that component that users use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 328.47,
          "end": 329.853,
          "en": "as it's the case here.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}